<title>ITALY: Italy's Turin sees Feb CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Turin sees Feb CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Turin said its February consumer price index stood at 0.1 percent month-on-month and 2.3 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In January, Turin's inflation rate was 0.0 percent and 2.6 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Turin is one of 11 Italian cities to have published inflation data Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 8.81 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to January 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.1    (0.0)    2.3  (2.6)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.2   (-0.3)    1.7  (2.2)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.4   (-0.1)    6.2  (5.8)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges  -1.2    (0.7)    1.9  (4.2)</p>
<p>    Furniture			  -0.1    (0.0)    1.7  (2.1)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.1    (1.8)    1.9  (1.7)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.4   (-0.3)    3.0  (2.8)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     1.0   (-1.4)    0.8  (0.9)</p>
<p>    Education			  -0.5    (0.0)    1.1  (2.0)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0    (0.0)    1.5  (1.7)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.1    (0.1)    2.3  (2.4)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
